    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "\"NOT clean\" is a verdict about the RUN, not about your diff",
      "prov:value": "That is not tidiness. The gates that ran after the mutation were handed the\nrepaired tree, so their verdicts describe a state you have not committed — bean\n`ymsu`, where `152 gate(s) pass` was printed **152 of 152 times** over a value\nnobody had committed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ymsu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Cause 2 — the artefact records the RUN, and your run differs",
      "prov:value": "### The worked example, and it is fixed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "The worked example, and it is fixed",
      "prov:value": "| | |\n|---|---|\n| **#1442** | pinned Bun in `.bun-version`, with `check:bun-pin` holding all 22 `oven-sh/setup-bun` sites to it. Makes **CI** consistent — and a container image is not something a repository can pin, so it could not reach an agent container. |\n| **#1452** | dropped `engine_version` from the comparison, joining the two `last_run_*` fields. Closes the residual: no engine difference rewrites anything. |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1442",
        "#1452"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The worked example, and it is fixed",
      "prov:value": "The owner kept both. They answer different halves: the pin makes the recorded\nengine consistent where the repository controls it, the skip stops any other\nengine from rewriting a file whose checker did not change."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The worked example, and it is fixed",
      "prov:value": "### The argument that decided it, because the wrong one is tempting"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The argument that decided it, because the wrong one is tempting",
      "prov:value": "---\n### The rule is convergent, not novel — and `3ozg` was the LAST family to get it",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3ozg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule is convergent, not novel — and `3ozg` was the LAST family to get it",
      "prov:value": "**What the sweep did not measure**, stated rather than implied: the 125 `block-qa`\nsidecars were verified by READING `qa-sweep.ts`'s guard, not by running it. `qa_sweep` is an MCP tool with no npm script and the platform carries no folio, so\nthere was no control to run. Six writers that could be run were, twice where\ncheap, and all were idempotent on a clean tree."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "If you meet a churn whose writer has not been fixed yet",
      "prov:value": "That is\n`sfjo`'s rule (*read what a regeneration writes before committing it*) applied to\na regeneration that is **faithful and still wrong to keep**: the generator records\nyour container correctly, and your container is not the repository."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "If you meet a churn whose writer has not been fixed yet",
      "prov:value": "**But discarding is a workaround, and the habit is the defect. `3ozg` was filed\n**three times in one day** — as `3ozg`, as `rmcf`, and `ymsu` is a different\ndefect over the same files — because every session that ran `bun run cat gates` on a\nclean tree saw the same always-red line, discarded the churn, and moved on. A signal that is always red is one nobody reads, and then it cannot report the\nnext real in-run repair, which is the whole reason the detector exists.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ymsu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/gate-tree-mutation.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Related",
      "prov:value": "| | |\n|---|---|\n| [`platform-gates`](platform-gates.md) | which gates to run, and cause 1 in full |\n| `scripts/gate-tree-guard.ts` | why the detector cannot live in a gate |\n| `pipeline/qa-utils.ts` | `saveQaScriptSidecar`'s comparison, with `3ozg`'s reasoning beside it |\n| [`generalise-the-fix`](generalise-the-fix.md) | the same shape one level up: fix the class, not the instance |\n| [`upstream-version-adoption`](upstream-version-adoption.md) | moving a pin forward — a person's decision, never a gate's |"
    }
  ]
